  {
    "title": "Gleim, Rothman Announce More Than $1 Million in LSA Funding for Local Projects",
    "url": "http://RepGleim.com/News/38733/Press-Releases/Gleim--Rothman-Announce-More-Than--1-Million-in-LSA-Funding-for-Local-Projects",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Gleim, Rothman Announce More Than $1 Million in LSA Funding for Local Projects\nSeptember 15, 2026\nHARRISBURG – State Sen. Greg Rothman (R-34) and Rep. Barb Gleim (R-Cumberland) are announcing more than $1 million in Local Share Account (LSA) funding that is being awarded to two projects in the 199th Legislative District.\n“These investments will have a direct and meaningful impact on our community,” said Gleim. “From ensuring our first responders have the equipment they need to protect public safety, to supporting an organization that provides valuable services to residents, these projects are worthy investments in the future of our area. I am pleased to have supported these funding requests and am grateful to see that they received approval.”\nThe West Pennsboro Township Fire Company plans to purchase a new mini pumper fire truck with the more than $427,000 grant it is receiving. Also, a $600,000 grant is being awarded to New Life Community Church for instillation of a new HVAC system that will allow it to better serve community groups.\n“I was pleased to advocate for this grant funding to keep our community safe and well supported,” Rothman added. “These state investments equip our local first responders and help ensure important needs are met within our community.”\nThe Local Share Account (LSA) program provides funding for projects that promote economic development, community improvement and public interest projects across Pennsylvania.\nRepresentative Barb Gleim\n199th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nSenator Greg Rothman\n34th Legislative District\nPennsylvania State Senate\nMedia Contact: Scott Little\n717-260-6137\nslittle@pahousegop.com\nRepGleim.com / Facebook.com/RepGleim\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "State Rep. Barb Gleim and State Sen. Greg Rothman announced that two local organizations in the 199th Legislative District will receive a combined $1.027 million in state Local Share Account grants. West Pennsboro Township Fire Company will receive $427,000 for a new mini pumper fire truck, and New Life Community Church will receive $600,000 for a new HVAC system. The legislators supported these funding requests, which were approved through Pennsylvania's LSA program.",
      "action_type": "budget",
      "topics": [
        "public_safety",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
