    "title": "Gleim Disappointed by House Democrats’ Move to Avoid Voting on the Save Women’s Sports Act",
    "url": "https://www.repgleim.com/News/36456/Press-Releases/Gleim-Disappointed-by-House-Democrats--Move-to-Avoid-Voting-on-the-Save-Women-s-Sports-Act",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Gleim Disappointed by House Democrats’ Move to Avoid Voting on the Save Women’s Sports Act\nJuly 8, 2025\nHARRISBURG – State Rep. Barb Gleim (R-Cumberland), author of\nHouse Bill 158\n(the Protect Women’s Sports Act), issued the following statement after House Democrat leadership re-referred\nSenate Bill 9\n(the Save Women’s Sports Act), to the House Health Committee.\n“The decision by House Democrat leaders and members of the House Education Committee who voted in favor of shifting Senate Bill 9 to another committee are ignoring the voices of women and girls who deserve the protections it gives them. They are also turning a deaf ear to the voices of an overwhelming number of Pennsylvanians who do not want biological men participating in women’s sports.\n“House Democrats are disregarding President Donald Trump’s executive order which ‘oppose(s) male competitive participation in women’s sports more broadly.’ Furthermore, they are risking the ‘(rescindment of) all funds from educational programs that deprive women and girls of fair athletic opportunities.\n“This is an education issue which has everything to do with safety and maintaining opportunities for women athletes, while fulfilling the goals of Title IX. The majority party has no intention of moving Senate Bill 9 or my House Bill 158, and I’m disappointed with their decision to avoid taking up the legislation and thus disrespecting women and girls.”\nRepresentative Barb Gleim\n199th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "State Rep. Barb Gleim issued a statement criticizing House Democrats after the House Education Committee voted to re-refer Senate Bill 9, a bill that would restrict transgender girls and women from competing in female sports categories, to the House Health Committee rather than advancing it. Gleim, who has authored a similar bill, argues the procedural move is an attempt to avoid a floor vote. The bills in question have not passed or been signed into law.",
      "action_type": "statement",
