    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Gleim to Host Bridge Dedication Ceremony\nJune 27, 2025\nWHAT:\nState Rep. Barb Gleim (R-Cumberland) will host a ceremony to honor the memory of Maj. Gen. Harold “Harry” Greene, a 2002 graduate of the United States Army War College in Carlisle. Greene was killed on Aug. 5, 2014, in an attack while visiting Camp Qargha’s Marshal Fahim National Defense University in Kabul.\nDuring the ceremony, the Army Heritage Drive bridge which crosses Interstate 81 in Middlesex Township, Cumberland County, will be designated the Major General Harold “Harry” Greene Memorial Bridge.\nWHO:\nGleim will be joined by members of Greene’s family; Maj. Gen. John R. Pippy, Pennsylvania’s adjutant general; and several local elected officials.\nWHEN:\nSaturday, June 28, at 1 p.m.\nWHERE:\nU.S. Army Heritage and Education Center,\n950 Soldiers Drive, Carlisle\n.\nMedia contact:\nScott Little,\nSlittle@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "State Rep. Barb Gleim is hosting a bridge dedication ceremony on June 28, 2025, to name a bridge on Army Heritage Drive over Interstate 81 in Cumberland County after Maj. Gen. Harold 'Harry' Greene, a U.S. Army officer killed in Afghanistan in 2014. Greene's family and Pennsylvania military officials will attend the event at the U.S. Army Heritage and Education Center in Carlisle.",
